        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Squirrel Nut Zippers, Sponge\n- People: James \"Jimbo\" Mathus, Tom Maxwell, Katharine Whalen, Chris Phillips, Don Raleigh, Ken Mosher, Vinnie Dombroski, Mike Cross, Tim Cross, Joey Mazzola\n- Places: Chapel Hill, North Carolina, Detroit, Michigan\n- Topics: American bands, formation\n\nFacts:\n- Sponge is an American alternative rock band that was formed in 1991 in Detroit, Michigan, by Vinnie Dombroski, Mike Cross, Tim Cross, and Joey Mazzola.\n- Squirrel Nut Zippers is an American swing band that was formed in 1993 in Chapel Hill, North Carolina, by James \"Jimbo\" Mathus, Tom Maxwell, Katharine Whalen, Chris Phillips, Don Raleigh, and Ken Mosher.\n- James \"Jimbo\" Mathus and Tom Maxwell were identified with vocals and guitar in Squirrel Nut Zippers.\n- Katharine Whalen was identified with vocals, banjo, and ukulele in Squirrel Nut Zippers.\n- Chris Phillips played drums, and Don Raleigh played bass guitar, in Squirrel Nut Zippers.",
